In a recent conversation, James Rising received an email from Israel Oyeniyi, a prospective PhD student, expressing interest in joining his research group at the University of Delaware. Israel highlighted his background in fisheries, climate change impacts, and sustainable resource management, showcasing various experiences, including research and coordination in climate adaptation. James requested an email response to inform Israel that he is not taking students this year, while also acknowledging his qualifications and encouraging him to explore other opportunities. A professional draft response was prepared, clearly stating that no positions are available and wishing Israel success in his future endeavors.
